{
  "dom_id": "step-q14996",
  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226762/assets/64cd6ad79a422927e0ca2c4d954c45b288c411a443cdd69e1076e46c86b92a6b.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the **total** shaded area that lies between the polar curves $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$ and $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ),$ as shown above?",
  "worked_solution": "Consider the pair of petals in the first quadrant. First, we find the values of $\\theta $ at which the two curves intersect:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two solutions for $2\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ]:$\n\n$$\n2\\theta =0,\\pi \\,⟹\\,\\theta =0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nTo determine the inner function and the outer, let's draw an arrow from the origin that passes through the shaded region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226762/assets/8cf1f087dd4b630dbba62d2b506111c05bcf22f4d4175d0b487736af8b6df865.png)\n\nThe arrow\n\n- *enters* the region through the inner function $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ),$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the outer function $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).$\n\nTo find the area, we use the formula\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}([\\text{outer}]^{2}-[\\text{inner}]^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$\\,$ ${\\theta }_{1}=0,\\,$ and $\\,{\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}((3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )-4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total shaded area is\n\n$$\nA=4{A}_{1}=10{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
